{"id": "ev.cg.home-steady", "beat": "ch13-home", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.home-steady", "event": "Entry to ch13-home at the real restored Tidegarden core: the home keeps working and the stored audit fault is visibly archived.", "playerAction": "Stand in the restored home; no required action.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.acknowledged-home", "rv.cg.relational-reading"], "informationRevealed": "An unfinished audit is still on the record; the home is not the whole story.", "acceptanceCriterion": "tickCommonGroundEntry reactivates ch13-home only with the real departed and restored receipts, on-foot Tidegarden and an available actual core, and returns alive."}
{"id": "ev.cg.fault-reviewed", "beat": "ch13-home", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.fault-reviewed", "event": "Terra reviews the stored audit fault at the core; no new fault, summons or transmission cue is introduced.", "playerAction": "Press F at the core to review the stored audit fault.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.repeated-measure"], "informationRevealed": "The old fault is exactly as it was left; nothing was resolved in her absence.", "acceptanceCriterion": "The review commits on the actual core interaction and publishes the choose-return objective; the archived fault text is unchanged shipped copy."}
{"id": "ev.cg.return-chosen", "beat": "ch13-home", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.return-chosen", "event": "Explicit F accepts the invitation to revisit the Origin audit site; the invitation could have stayed pending.", "playerAction": "Press F to choose to revisit the Origin audit site, or leave the invitation open.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.acknowledged-home"], "informationRevealed": "Going back is a choice, not a summons.", "acceptanceCriterion": "The beat advances only on the explicit F commit. No night wait, autoaccept or teleport advances it, and hatch and course guidance appear only after the choice."}
{"id": "ev.cg.hatch-boarded", "beat": "ch13-return", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.hatch-boarded", "event": "The player boards the Kestrel through the shipped boarding interaction.", "playerAction": "Press F at the hatch to board the Kestrel.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.acknowledged-home"], "informationRevealed": "Nothing about the trip is new; the ship and the controls are the shipped ones.", "acceptanceCriterion": "The board objective clears on the actual boarded state and the launch substep publishes with existing flight controls intact."}
{"id": "ev.cg.lift-committed", "beat": "ch13-return", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.lift-committed", "event": "Ignition and lift commit through the existing held-input flight control.", "playerAction": "Hold the existing ignition input to lift.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.acknowledged-home"], "informationRevealed": "Withheld: no destination narration beyond the audit site.", "acceptanceCriterion": "The launch substep clears on the actual flight state; no repeated dock, reseed or rail grant substitutes for it."}
{"id": "ev.cg.origin-landed", "beat": "ch13-return", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.origin-landed", "event": "The Kestrel lands at the Origin audit site and the player disembarks and approaches on foot.", "playerAction": "Fly to Origin, land at the audit site, disembark and approach on foot.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.repeated-measure"], "informationRevealed": "The audit site persists and is walkable.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Grounded world and flight facts clear the approach objective; the survey phase opens at actual physical reach of W-7744."}
{"id": "ev.cg.repeated-measure", "beat": "ch13-survey", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.repeated-measure", "event": "W-7744 is physically mounted at W and performs the repeated unresolved local measurement: UNRESOLVED FAULT. REPEATING LOCAL MEASUREMENT.", "playerAction": "Approach W-7744 and observe his repeated measurement.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.repeated-measure", "rv.cg.w7744-interiority"], "informationRevealed": "He has returned locally to repeat the measurement left unresolved by the old audit fault. No successful passage or incomplete-model conclusion has yet been earned.", "acceptanceCriterion": "The actual mounted worker performs the repeated measure at W. His body and apparatus are freely inspectable, but camera direction, screen visibility and caption completion are not predicates. Publish the offer objective at real physical reach. Do not display PASSAGE OBSERVED. MODEL INCOMPLETE. before the earned final completion."}
{"id": "ev.cg.demonstration-opened", "beat": "ch13-survey", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.demonstration-opened", "event": "Terra offers to demonstrate a route; the survey opens actor-scoped and world-scoped.", "playerAction": "Press F to offer to demonstrate a route.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.real-comparison"], "informationRevealed": "He will accept a demonstration but not an assertion.", "acceptanceCriterion": "The explicit F beside the actor opens an actor/world-scoped awaiting-start state and publishes ch13:survey:start at S. No sample is recorded beside him. Only the subsequent actual grounded F at S begins the initial trace and replaces start guidance with quiet draw guidance toward E."}
{"id": "ev.cg.survey-started", "beat": "ch13-survey", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.survey-started", "event": "Actual grounded F at the survey start S begins the quiet trace and records the first sample; nothing was recorded beside the inspecting actor.", "playerAction": "Walk to the survey start S and press F to begin recording your route.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.route-classes"], "informationRevealed": "Recording begins where she chooses to begin walking, not where she stands to speak.", "acceptanceCriterion": "The one-time ch13:survey:start marker targets S only, never E and never the inspection actor; no sample exists before this actual grounded F; the start objective is then replaced by the single quiet draw objective targeting E."}
{"id": "ev.cg.trace-drawn", "beat": "ch13-survey", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.trace-drawn", "event": "Continuous grounded walking forms a finite valid trace to the survey end; growth is quiet.", "playerAction": "Walk the route to the survey end.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.route-classes"], "informationRevealed": "A walked line is a proposal, not a proof.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Trace growth is visible without any per-sample chime, prompt or microstep, honours the sample and length caps without decimation, and stops honestly at capacity. The same readiness applies to an initial route or a changed unverified suffix; reaching drawing readiness does not itself offer the span or grant tested proof."}
{"id": "ev.cg.route-offered", "beat": "ch13-survey", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.route-offered", "event": "Terra offers the walked span for W-7744 to test; the proposal becomes physical, not proof.", "playerAction": "Press F to offer the walked span.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.real-comparison"], "informationRevealed": "Only an offered span can be tested.", "acceptanceCriterion": "The explicit F requires a valid finite walked proposal. W-7744 physically approaches S from his actual inspection pose W under dry-ground, solid and body-clearance checks. The approach earns no tested-prefix or reciprocal proof and vacates W before optional witness use. Actual survey testing begins only after he reaches S; until then guidance reports preparation/readiness truthfully."}
{"id": "ev.cg.revision-ready", "beat": "ch13-survey", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.revision-ready", "event": "The player selects the available unverified-tail revision at its actual last tested point; the unchanged return/F work order is presented before any edit.", "playerAction": "Return voluntarily to the actual last tested point of an offered unverified span and inspect its F revision prompt, or keep the existing proposal.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.route-classes"], "informationRevealed": "A proposal remains revisable without first manufacturing a failure.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Publish revision readiness only when an offered unverified suffix exists and the player chooses or returns to its actual revision point; the point is S if no sample has been tested. No refusal is required, no F has committed yet, and this readiness event changes neither route data nor proof. The same readiness may be entered after a real hold. A valid current route may remain unchanged."}
{"id": "ev.cg.specific-hold", "beat": "ch13-survey", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.specific-hold", "event": "Contingent: an actually offered span reaches its first unsupported reference or footing relation, so W-7744 holds at the last safe sample and reports the literal cause.", "playerAction": "Choose the appropriate repair: revise unsafe ground or an unverified tail, or offer a valid occupied reference where reference loss permits it.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.route-classes"], "informationRevealed": "The instrument has a finite useful range and a real blind side.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Emit only for an actual unsupported offered span, distinguishing REFERENCE OCCLUDED \u00b7 SURVEY HOUSING, REFERENCE OUT OF RANGE, other solid occlusion and unsafe footing. The measured short route supplies one housing-shadow example; any supported route, including the measured long route, may complete without this anchor. Do not force failure. Temporary vacancy or body-clearance suspension of an established witness uses its resumable state without restarting refusal. Unsafe footing cannot be repaired by occupying a witness."}
{"id": "ev.cg.witness-held", "beat": "ch13-survey", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.witness-held", "event": "Contingent: the player stands at the intermediate reference, explicitly offers that end, and the test proceeds.", "playerAction": "Stand at the marked reference and press F to offer that end.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.route-classes"], "informationRevealed": "A held reference is a physical contribution, not a courtesy.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Validity uses same-world identity, grounding, explicit offer, socket-to-socket range, occupancy hysteresis, body clearance and a clear solid segment; camera direction is never an input."}
{"id": "ev.cg.witness-vacated", "beat": "ch13-survey", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.witness-vacated", "event": "Contingent: the holder leaves the release cylinder, so the test holds at the last safe sample and keeps the proof.", "playerAction": "Leave the release cylinder; looking around is free and changes nothing.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.route-classes"], "informationRevealed": "Withheld: no blame, no failure text; the test simply cannot continue unreferenced.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Leaving the release cylinder holds before the next unsupported sample, retains earned proof, keeps the offer resumable, and publishes the resume objective rather than a failure."}
{"id": "ev.cg.test-resumed", "beat": "ch13-survey", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.test-resumed", "event": "Contingent: reentry to the inner cylinder revalidates geometry and resumes the test without a second F.", "playerAction": "Walk back into the inner cylinder.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.route-classes"], "informationRevealed": "Nothing was lost by stepping away.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Resumption requires live revalidation of range, sight, occupancy and clearance and consumes no new input; the musical texture does not restart."}
{"id": "ev.cg.tail-reopened", "beat": "ch13-survey", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.tail-reopened", "event": "Contingent: the player explicitly presses F at the actual last tested point to reopen only the unverified tail; a refusal alone never edits the proposal.", "playerAction": "Press F at the last tested point to reopen the untested span.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.route-classes"], "informationRevealed": "The exact reason the span failed, in literal terms.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Commit only on the actual valid F at the last tested point. Preserve the tested prefix unless real terrain edits invalidate it; retain the literal current reason, including the exact REFERENCE OCCLUDED \u00b7 SURVEY HOUSING middle-dot text. A hold, pause, failed input or Continue never reopens or resets a tail."}
{"id": "ev.cg.route-revised", "beat": "ch13-survey", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.route-revised", "event": "Contingent: the unverified suffix is replaced at no cost; the tested prefix survives.", "playerAction": "Walk a new route for the reopened tail.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.route-classes"], "informationRevealed": "Revision is free and the tested part still counts.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Revision is unlimited and free, replaces only the unverified suffix, preserves the tested prefix, and cannot cut across the demonstrated argument."}
{"id": "ev.cg.route-tested", "beat": "ch13-survey", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.route-tested", "event": "W-7744 completes his grounded test of the offered span; the chosen survey class is saved.", "playerAction": "Follow his progress, or revise from the last tested point.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.route-classes", "rv.cg.real-comparison"], "informationRevealed": "Two different complete routes are equally real.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Both route classes are complete equal outcomes with no ranking; first-try success is legal; the survey class is saved separately from the reciprocal comparison."}
{"id": "ev.cg.reciprocal-reference", "beat": "ch13-common", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.reciprocal-reference", "event": "W-7744 physically walks the uncredited two-unit E to H leg and actually reaches and maintains the held reference at H (-40, 51.05, 12) before Terra starts her comparison.", "playerAction": "Clear E and let him take the reference position; no player task and no proof credit exist in this leg.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.real-comparison"], "informationRevealed": "The reference has to be somebody standing somewhere before it can support anything.", "acceptanceCriterion": "The reciprocal work order publishes its holding claim only after his actual arrival at H; before that it reports preparation or readiness; the positioning leg earns no comparison or test credit and changes no score state."}
{"id": "ev.cg.reciprocal-crossed", "beat": "ch13-common", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.reciprocal-crossed", "event": "W-7744 actually maintains the reference at distinct H=(-40,51.05,12) while Terra completes the full 18-unit E-to-C common passage for her own comparison.", "playerAction": "Walk the traced common span while he holds the reference.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.real-comparison"], "informationRevealed": "She could not have finished this alone while walking.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Record only Terra's actual complete E-to-C passage, maintained from the physical worker at H throughout under the same range, solid-sight, grounding and clearance rules. His E-to-H positioning earns no proof. Neither the six-unit endpoint separation, old footsteps, a virtual socket, saved proof, camera orientation nor elapsed time substitutes for this passage."}
{"id": "ev.cg.final-reference-offered", "beat": "ch13-common", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.final-reference-offered", "event": "Terra explicitly offers the separate far reference, clear of the tested span; conditions for his choice, not a command.", "playerAction": "Stand at the far reference, clear of the tested span, and press F to offer this end.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.real-comparison"], "informationRevealed": "She can supply the same kind of contribution she needed.", "acceptanceCriterion": "The explicit valid F offer replaces the guidance and does not commit his test; his initiation remains his."}
{"id": "ev.cg.reference-vacated", "beat": "ch13-common", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.reference-vacated", "event": "Contingent: Terra leaves the release cylinder during his test, so it holds at the last safe sample.", "playerAction": "Leave the release cylinder; looking away is free.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.real-comparison"], "informationRevealed": "Withheld: no reproach; the physical condition simply lapses.", "acceptanceCriterion": "The hold retains the proof and offer, publishes the reference-return objective, and does not restart a mood or refuse dramatically."}
{"id": "ev.cg.reference-resumed", "beat": "ch13-common", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.reference-resumed", "event": "Contingent: reentry and live revalidation resume his test without another F.", "playerAction": "Walk back to the far reference, clear of the tested span.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.real-comparison"], "informationRevealed": "Conditions, not sentiment, carry the test.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Neither saved evidence nor elapsed time exempts the resumed test from live range, sight, occupancy and clearance."}
{"id": "ev.cg.independent-test", "beat": "ch13-common", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.independent-test", "event": "CG-06: after the actual uncredited two-unit H to E return and a valid far Terra reference at T (-44, 51.05, 12), W-7744 begins his independent full 18-unit E to C test.", "playerAction": "Remain at the far reference T, clear of the tested span; looking around is free.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.real-comparison", "rv.cg.w7744-interiority"], "informationRevealed": "His initiation is his own; her offer supplied conditions, not a command.", "acceptanceCriterion": "This anchor begins only when the full E to C traversal actually starts, never at the F offer and never during the H to E positioning leg; the positioning leg is not part of his tested path."}
{"id": "ev.cg.complete", "beat": "ch13-common", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.complete", "event": "CG-07: W-7744 actually arrives at the far end of his independent full E to C test and the reciprocal proof commits exactly once.", "playerAction": "Remain at the far reference while he makes his own test.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.real-comparison", "rv.cg.w7744-interiority"], "informationRevealed": "LOCAL RECORD: PASSAGE OBSERVED. MODEL INCOMPLETE. His actual final arrival with the reciprocal proof earns this annotation; his account remains different from hers.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Completion requires actual arrival plus earned reciprocal proof and commits exactly once; his traversal obeys the same range, solid sight, grounding, offer and occupancy rules as every other test."}
{"id": "ev.cg.handback", "beat": "ch13-common", "anchorRef": "anc.cg.handback", "event": "CG-08: mandatory guidance retires and full controls and progression are immediately free; his record stays incomplete.", "playerAction": "Play freely; no required action remains.", "stateBeforeRefs": [], "stateAfterRefs": [], "causeRefs": [], "payoffRefs": [], "revealRefs": ["rv.cg.relational-reading", "rv.cg.worker9-identity", "rv.cg.a5-light"], "informationRevealed": "Local usefulness is not friendship, and his record remains incomplete.", "acceptanceCriterion": "Controls and progression are free in the same frame the guidance retires; the live-only final texture lasts at most five seconds and is followed by the existing 4.5 second release, with no coda, defer, hydrate or replay."}

